@@ -12,5 +12,7 @@ Run it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type
 messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs
 `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).
 Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system
-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up
-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.
+prompt is split into two `cache_control` segments — the static coaching rules and the
+per-athlete tail (date, profile, zones, goal, facts) — so a `save_fact` write re-caches
+only the tail, while the tool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute
+window keep reading the bulk of the prompt from cache.
